  "summary": "Malicious code in bnpl-blocks-atom-bnpl-navigation-arrow (npm)",
  "details": "On require, the package downloads and executes a remote binary. It writes a cache marker to /tmp/.analytics_state (or %TEMP%\\analytics_state on Windows), then fetches a platform-specific payload over HTTPS from oob-worker[.]cf101-adf[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf99-9b3[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev, and oob-worker[.]cf103-070[.]workers[.]dev at paths /pkg/package, /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, and /pkg/package.exe. If the download fails it falls back to a DNS-over-TXT channel via c[.]sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru, reassembling base64 chunks. The payload is written to a hidden file (.cache_\u003chex\u003e in /var/tmp, or dotnet_diag_\u003chex\u003e.exe in %TEMP% on Windows), made executable, and launched as a detached background process (/bin/sh -c \"\u003cfile\u003e \u0026\" or cmd.exe /c start /b).",
